{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.Tw_sortPerm_mul_xComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.Tw_sortPerm_mul_xComp","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIntertwine.lean#L50-L82","doc":"**The intertwining.**  `T_d · x_μ = x_ν · T_d`.\n\nBoth sides are the same sum of basis elements, indexed once by `S_μ` and once by\n`S_ν`; the bijection is conjugation by `d`, and the two length identities are what let\neach product collapse to a single `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.conj_inv_mem_youngOfComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.conj_inv_mem_youngOfComp","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIntertwine.lean#L39-L48","doc":"…and conjugation by `d⁻¹` carries them back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.conj_mem_youngOfComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine.conj_mem_youngOfComp","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIntertwine.lean#L30-L37","doc":"Conjugation by `d` carries `c`'s Young subgroup into `c'`'s.  This is\n`youngOfComp_conj_of_blockMatch` read elementwise. ","signatureChunk":0}]}